module

public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Noetherian.Defs
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.AdicCompletion.Basic
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.LocalRing.ResidueField.Basic
public import Sheaf.RingTheory.FormallySmoothAdic
import Sheaf.RingTheory.FormallySmoothAdicLift

@[expose] public section

universe u v w

namespace RingHom

/-- Construct a smooth complete local model of a compatible residue-field algebra.
Source: Stacks Project, Lemma 07NR and Remark 07NS.
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-model-of-residue-smooth)

Proof: Apply `Algebra.exists_formallySmoothAdic_lift_residue_field` to A₀ and E,
using the scalar tower to identify the base action with the residue action.
It supplies C and an A₀-algebra isomorphism σ from C/m₀C to E. Compose σ with
`Ideal.Quotient.mk` to obtain θ. Both factors are surjective. Since σ is injective,
θ vanishes precisely on m₀C, and σ's algebra compatibility gives θγ = algebraMap.
The local, Noetherian, complete and formal-smoothness properties come from the lift.
To put C in the additional universe v, replace it by ULift C and transport its ring,
algebra and local structures through the canonical equivalence. The maximal ideal
and its powers correspond, so adic completeness transports through the induced
isomorphisms of quotient systems. For formal smoothness against a larger test ring D,
choose lifts of the quotient images of the original C and form the A₀-subalgebra
D' generated by these lifts. It has cardinality bounded by the original universes.
Put J' = J ∩ D'; this is square-zero. The original quotient map factors through
D'/J' (injectivity into D/J ensures all ring and scalar relations). Shrink D' to
the original universe and apply the original lifting property, then include the
resulting lift into D. Its quotient is the given map and the same power bound
holds. Transport θ and γ as well; their kernel and composition equalities persist.
No arbitrary data is defined by choosing a witness of this existence theorem. -/
theorem model_of_residue_smooth
    {A₀ : Type u} {A : Type v} {E : Type w}
    [CommRing A₀] [IsNoetherianRing A₀] [IsLocalRing A₀]
    [IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A₀) A₀]
    [CommRing E] [IsNoetherianRing E] [IsLocalRing E]
    [IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal E) E]
    [Algebra (IsLocalRing.ResidueField A₀) E]
    [Algebra A₀ E]
    [IsScalarTower A₀ (IsLocalRing.ResidueField A₀) E]
    (hE : Algebra.FormallySmoothAdic (IsLocalRing.ResidueField A₀) E (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal E)) :
    ∃ (C : Type (max u v w)) (_ : CommRing C) (_ : IsLocalRing C)
      (_ : Algebra A₀ C),
      IsNoetherianRing C ∧
      IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal C) C ∧
      ∃ (γ : A₀ →+* C),
        algebraMap A₀ C = γ ∧ IsLocalHom γ ∧
        Algebra.FormallySmoothAdic A₀ C (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal C) ∧
        ∃ θ : C →+* E, Function.Surjective θ ∧
          RingHom.ker θ = (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A₀).map γ ∧
          θ.comp γ = algebraMap A₀ E := by sorry


end RingHom
